  "text": "Jackson County Board of Elections\nHome\nELECTIONS INFORMATION\nAbsentee Voting By Mail\nEarly Voting\nElection Day\nElection Notices\nSample Ballot\nElection Security\nResults & Data\nVoter Registration\nVoter Registration\nMy Voter Info\nYouth & University Voting\nVoter Photo ID\nPhoto ID\nPhoto ID Requirements\nGet Involved!\nMeetings & Events\nBeing a Precinct Official\nMore\nHome\nELECTIONS INFORMATION\nAbsentee Voting By Mail\nEarly Voting\nElection Day\nElection Notices\nSample Ballot\nElection Security\nResults & Data\nVoter Registration\nVoter Registration\nMy Voter Info\nYouth & University Voting\nVoter Photo ID\nPhoto ID\nPhoto ID Requirements\nGet Involved!\nMeetings & Events\nBeing a Precinct Official\nSign In\nMy Account\nSigned in as:\nfiller@godaddy.com\nMy Account\nSign out\nSigned in as:\nfiller@godaddy.com\nHome\nELECTIONS INFORMATION\nAbsentee Voting By Mail\nEarly Voting\nElection Day\nElection Notices\nSample Ballot\nElection Security\nResults & Data\nVoter Registration\nVoter Registration\nMy Voter Info\nYouth & University Voting\nVoter Photo ID\nPhoto ID\nPhoto ID Requirements\nGet Involved!\nMeetings & Events\nBeing a Precinct Official\nAccount\nMy Account\nSign out\nSign In\nMy Account\n876 Skyland Drive, Sylva, NC 28779 828.586.7538 ElectionsInfo@JacksonNC.org\n876 Skyland Drive, Sylva, NC 28779 828.586.7538 ElectionsInfo@JacksonNC.org\n876 Skyland Drive, Sylva, NC 28779 828.586.7538 ElectionsInfo@JacksonNC.org\n876 Skyland Drive, Sylva, NC 28779 828.586.7538 ElectionsInfo@JacksonNC.org\n876 Skyland Drive, Sylva, NC 28779 828.586.7538 ElectionsInfo@JacksonNC.org\n876 Skyland Drive, Sylva, NC 28779 828.586.7538 ElectionsInfo@JacksonNC.org\nNorth Carolina Photo ID Requirement for Voting\nUpdates from the BOE\n2026 General Election Sample Ballots are AVAILABLE!\nPrinted sample ballots for the 2026 General Election are available now!\nClick HERE to view a Jackson Co. sample ballot.\nUtilize the\nVoter Search Tool\nto look up your voter information and see your precinct ballot. (This tool is updated daily and the ballots may not appear until 9.3.26)\nPrinted copies are available at the BOE Office\nPrinted copies are available at every voting location.\nYou may see campaigners sharing sample ballots. These ballots should be clearly marked in a way indicating they are not live, official ballots. If they are pre-marked samples, they should include a statement about \"Paid for by...\", \"Authorized by...\" or \"Not authorized..\" statements.\nIt is important to do your research ahead of time - start now!\nThe Office of the NC Secretary of State and NC State Board of Elections provide voter research materials for certain statewide ballot items.\nOfficial Summary Explanation of 2026 Constitutional Amendments Released by Legislative Services Officer\n(Press release by NC Secretary of State\nJudicial Voter Guide: 2026 Election\n(Press release by NC State Board of Elections)\nNote: All Jackson Co. contests are the same across all precincts; ballots are just organized with labels based on the voter's precinct. For example: If you see a sample for Barker's Creek, the exact same contests/layout will be on the ballot for Caney Fork etc.\nJackson County's Newest \"I Voted\" Sticker!\nWe received almost 40 youth submissions for Jackson County's 2026 \"I Voted\" sticker! Thanks, artists!\nAnd nearly 300 members of the public voted to choose their favorite design!\nAt the August 4 meeting of the Jackson Co. Board of Commissioners, we announced our top three finalists and the winning design!\n3rd place: Miller Solsbee, age 8\n2nd place: Lincoln Brooks, age 8\nWinner: Naomi Pratt, age 7\nThe top three finalists will all receive certificates and local business prize packs at an upcoming Board of Elections meeting.\nCongratulations to the artists!\nNaomi's design will be available for voters at all Jackson Co. voting sites (while supplies last). Come vote to receive your custom sticker!\nFREE Voter Photo IDs from the BOE\nFREE Voter Photo IDs from the BOE\nAll NC voters are asked to provide a photo ID when voting. Most voters have an NC driver's license or other\nacceptable form of photo ID\n.\nRegistered voters can receive a FREE voter photo ID at their county BOE office.\nNo special documents are needed, you do not have to make an appointment & oftentimes, IDs can be issued on-the-spot within a few minutes! Voters simply complete an ID request form with basic information and have their photo taken; an ID is provided over-the-counter immediately or by-mail. Such IDs are\ncompletely free\nand can be used when voting for ten years!\nIf you would like a voter photo ID, visit the Jackson Co. BOE office or outreach event to complete a request form and have your picture taken.\nMore info on NC voter photo ID requirements are available HERE.\n2026 Election Day Polls Open\nElection Day is approaching fast! Make sure you're ready to vote!\nCheck your voter registration TODAY at\nhttps://vt.ncsbe.gov/RegLkup/\n0\n0\nDays\nDays\n0\n0\nHrs\nHours\n0\n0\nMins\nMinutes\n0\n0\nSecs\nSeconds\n2026 Statewide General Election\nSBE Candidate Guide & filing info sheet are available below. Specific candidate resources are available from the State Board of Elections. For Candidate information, visit:\nhttps://www.ncsbe.gov/candidates.\nCandidate lists are updated daily and available online; visit\nhttps://www.ncsbe.gov/results-data/candidate-lists.\nGeneral information for voters - dates, deadlines etc. - is available below.\nSample ballots will be available in late summer. Check yours using the\nSBE Voter Search tool.\nA Candidate's Guide to 2025-26 Statewide Primary & General Elections\n(pdf)\nDownload\n2026 General Election Info Flyer\n(jpg)\nDownload\n11.3.2026 Candidate List Grouped by Contest\n(pdf)\nDownload\nElections Results\nSeeking information about elections? Reporting of unofficial election results does not begin until polls close on Election Day.\nClick the button below to utilize the State Board of Elections results dashboard which includes live & historical (thru 2010) data.\nSBE ELECTION RESULTS DASHBOARD\nAbout Us\nOffice Staff:\nAmanda Allen, Director\nAmandaAllen@JacksonNC.org\nDaniel Landa, Elections Operations Manager\nDanielLanda@JacksonNC.org\nShannon Quinn, Elections Data Manager\nShannonQuinn@JacksonNC.org\nKylee Muench, Elections Specialist\nKyleeMuench@JacksonNC.org\nBoard Members:\nBill Thompson: Chair\nBillThompson@JacksonNC.org\nDavid Brooks: Board Member\nDavidBrooks@JacksonNC.org\nRoy Osborn: Board Member\nRoyOsborn@JacksonNC.org\nJay Pavey: Board Member\nJayPavey@JacksonNC.org\nBetsy Swift: Secretary\nBetsySwift@JacksonNC.org\nJackson County Board of Elections\nOffice Location: 876 Skyland Drive Suite 1, Sylva, NC 28779\nMailing:\n401\nGrindstaff Cove Road, Sylva, NC\n28779\n(828) 586-7538\n//\nElectionsInfo@JacksonNC.org\nHours\nMon\n08:00 am \u2013 05:00 pm\nTue\n08:00 am \u2013 05:00 pm\nWed\n08:00 am \u2013 05:00 pm\nThu\n08:00 am \u2013 05:00 pm\nFri\n08:00 am \u2013 05:00 pm\nSat\nClosed\nSun\nClosed\nLike & Follow Jackson County NC Board of Elections\nCopyright \u00a9 2020 Jackson County Board of Elections - All Rights Reserved\nPowered by",
